options.description:
Text transformations applied to register contents before substitution. Can be a list of modifier names or a function that returns a list based on context. Available modifiers: 'linewise' (force new line), 'reindent' (fix indentation), 'trim' (strip whitespace), 'join' (collapse to one line). Leave as nil to use register contents as-is.

Example (array): { 'trim', 'reindent' }
Example (function): function(state) return { 'trim' } end

Advanced: override what text is used as the substitution subject. Accepts a string motion (e.g. 'iw'), a function returning a string, or a table with a 'motion' key. Leave as nil to use the default behavior (word under cursor or visual selection).

Example: 'iw'
Example: { motion = 'iw' }

Advanced: override the line range for substitution. Accepts a string motion (e.g. 'ip'), a function, or a table with an 'expand' key. Leave as nil to use the default behavior (motion after first keypress).

Example: 'ip'
Example: { expand = '<cword>' }
